    "3": {
      "note": "Readiness also derives a part map: claims require resolving bases and unique part ownership; `data-evidence-claim` carries actual claim IDs while `data-evidence` retains its separate basis-reference check. A page without explicit parts is one implicit `page` part containing its real claims, with whole-page staleness rather than invented part IDs.\n\nAnchor: `test_readiness_requires_resolving_claim_bases_and_unique_part_ownership`, `test_claim_ids_and_the_legacy_reference_check_stay_separate`, `test_a_page_without_parts_is_ready_as_one_implicit_part_with_real_claim_ids`",
